      "h3": null,
      "h4": null,
      "h5": null,
      "text": "15 January 2015"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "h2": null,
      "h3": null,
      "h4": null,
      "h5": null,
      "text": "Did you know that full-time employees in the UK earned £528 per week on average in 2015, and that on average women earned 9.4% less than men per hour? These earnings varied greatly across the UK, with City of London employees earning the highest at £921 and employees in North East Derbyshire earning the lowest at £389."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "h2": null,
      "h3": null,
      "h4": null,
      "h5": null,
      "text": "There are plenty more interesting facts to explore by region, using our [cartogram](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cartogram) below to uncover stories of your own. You can even change the jobs sector and see how the shape of the country changes as a result."
    },
